<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mesannepadda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 2500 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/26th-century-bce">26th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mesannepadda was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ur">Ur</a> around 2500 BCE, named in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumerian-king-list">Sumerian King List</a> as the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-babylonian-empire">First Dynasty</a> of Ur. His name appears on contemporary objects, including a seal from the Royal Cemetery of Ur and a bead found at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mari">Mari</a>, and he also bore the title king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kish">Kish</a>, claiming wider supremacy in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumer">Sumer</a>. He is one of the earliest Sumerian kings whose existence is confirmed by contemporary sources.</p></div>
